  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Given, the point&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>&alpha;</mi></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>&beta;</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;be at a unit distance from each of the two lines&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>:</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>12</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>, and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>:</mo><mn>8</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>11</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>, so on plotting the diagram we get,</p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0074_3dc048a1e7c2.png\" style=\"width: 244px; height: 300px;\" />​​​​​​​</p><p>Now,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>:</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>12</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>:</mo><mn>8</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>11</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p>Since <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>&amp;</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;are perpendicular so it will form square of unit length, so equation of angle bisector of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;of angle containing origin and will pass through&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>&alpha;</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>&beta;</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>, so</p><p>Equation of angle bisector will be,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>12</mn></mrow></mfenced><msqrt><msup><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mn>4</mn><mn>2</mn></msup></msqrt></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>8</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>11</mn></mrow><msqrt><msup><mn>8</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mn>6</mn><mn>2</mn></msup></msqrt></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&rArr;</mo><mn>2</mn><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>12</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>11</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&rArr;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>14</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>13</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&rArr;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>&alpha;</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>14</mn><mi>&beta;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>13</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>⋯</mo><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi></mfenced></math></p><p>Also given perpendicular distance is one unit so,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>&alpha;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>&beta;</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>12</mn></mrow><mn>5</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&rArr;</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>&alpha;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>&beta;</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>⋯</mo><mfenced><mi>ii</mi></mfenced></math></p><p>Solving equation&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mtext>i</mtext></mfenced><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>&amp;</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mfenced><mtext>ii</mtext></mfenced></math></p><p>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>&alpha;</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>14</mn><mi>&beta;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>13</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mi>&alpha;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>&beta;</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&rArr;</mo></math><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>&alpha;</mi></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>&beta;</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mi>&alpha;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>23</mn></mrow><mn>25</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mi>&beta;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>53</mn><mn>50</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>So,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>100</mn><mfenced><mrow><mi>&alpha;</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>&beta;</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>14</mn></math></p></blockquote>"
  }
